  "subtitle": "Petrie Sculpture Court",
  "blurb": "A sunlit indoor courtyard: a peaked glass roof over pale stone and red brick, and light off every surface.",
  "corridorNote": "Modelled on the Carroll and Milton Petrie European Sculpture Court by day. A great peaked skylight of white steel and glass roofs what reads as an outdoor courtyard wedged between two buildings, with a lower run of flat glazing along the eaves; daylight floods the room and lies in bars across the paving. One wall is smooth pale stone with arched openings and illuminated panels, the other a facade of dark red brick set with white stone arches and circular medallions. A floor-to-ceiling glass wall closes the far end. The court's own sculpture is left out here: this exhibition is about the paintings.",
